; Binds `(form-arity f)` to `:impl "wasm:form_arity"` and
; `(forms-arity-sum v)` to `:impl "wasm:forms_arity_sum"` — the
; sibling double.wasm exports both functions. `form-arity` accepts
; one form arg and returns `children_count + kvpair_count`;
; `forms-arity-sum` accepts a vector-of-form arg and returns the sum
; of each form's arity. Used by §18's form round-trip stretch case
; to prove `Tag.form` (`0x07`) crosses the plugin boundary intact,
; both bare and inside `Tag.vector`.
;
; `point` and `vec` are registered as forms so the validator
; recognises the heads — without these schemas the document would
; fire `unknown_form` before reaching the evaluator. The plugin
; itself doesn't care about field names (it just reads counts), so
; the schemas declare the minimum shape the test inputs use.
(plugin :name double :version "1.0.0"

  (form :name point
    (key :name x :type number :optional false)
    (key :name y :type number :optional false)
    (key :name z :type number :optional false))

  (form :name vec
    (key :name x :type number :optional false)
    (key :name y :type number :optional false))

  (expr-func :name form-arity
    :arity (fixed 1)
    :params [form]
    :result number
    :impl "wasm:form_arity")

  (expr-func :name forms-arity-sum
    :arity (fixed 1)
    :params [vector]
    :result number
    :impl "wasm:forms_arity_sum"))
